B.Co=new A.bd("A logic grid puzzle looks like a table and plays like a conversation with yourself. You are told a handful of facts, and everything else has to be worked out \u2014 nothing is hidden and nothing is guessed.",!1)
B.Cz=new A.bd("Each case has a small cast and two or three things to pin on them: what each person had, where each was seen, and sometimes when. Every person matches exactly one item in each column, and no two people share the same one.",!1)
B.Cu=new A.bd("The clues never lie, and they are never enough on their own. They are enough together.",!1)
B.Ev=s([B.Co,B.Cz,B.Cu],t.T9)
B.BV=new A.iG("What is a logic grid puzzle?",B.Ev)
B.Cf=new A.bd("Marking the grid",!0)
B.C_=new A.bd("Tap a cell once to rule it out \u2014 these two do not go together. Tap it again to confirm it. Tap a third time to clear it.",!1)
B.C9=new A.bd("When you confirm a cell, the rest of its row and column are ruled out for you. Only empty cells are filled this way; a cross you placed yourself is never touched. Take a confirmation back and the crosses it produced go with it.",!1)
B.Ck=new A.bd("The clue list",!0)
B.C8=new A.bd("Tap a clue to strike it through once you have squeezed it dry. Tap again to bring it back. Nothing is lost.",!1)
B.Ce=new A.bd("The tools",!0)
B.CE=new A.jZ(B.lu,"The story again \u2014 who, what was taken, and where")
B.CH=new A.jZ(B.lB,"Undo, one step at a time, including a whole-grid clear")
B.CG=new A.jZ(B.lv,"Check your marks, erase mistakes, or ask for the next move")
B.CF=new A.jZ(B.lx,"Clear the grid, fit it back to the screen, the theme, and this guide")
B.Cy=new A.bd("Moving around a big grid",!0)
B.Cb=new A.bd("Casual cases fit the screen. Larger ones do not \u2014 pinch to zoom in, drag to move around, and use Fit the grid to see it all again. The whole grid is always drawn; zooming only changes how close you stand.",!1)
B.Cw=new A.bd("Closing the case",!0)
B.Cs=new A.bd("When your grid places someone at the scene, tap Name who was responsible \u2014 it reads the name straight off your own grid and asks you to confirm it.",!1)
B.C4=new A.bd("There is no list to choose from, and that is deliberate: a list of four names would let anyone close a case by guessing, and nothing here is meant to be won by guessing. If your grid does not put anybody at the scene yet, the app simply says so. Nothing is counted against you.",!1)
B.EY=s([B.Cf,B.C_,B.C9,B.Ck,B.C8,B.Ce,B.CE,B.CH,B.CG,B.CF,B.Cy,B.Cb,B.Cw,B.Cs,B.C4],t.T9)
B.BX=new A.iG("How to play",B.EY)
B.Ct=new A.bd('A clue usually says more than it seems to. "The one who had the seed tin was seen at the millpond" fixes nothing on its own, but it rules out the seed tin for everyone not at the millpond, and the millpond for everyone without the seed tin. One sentence, two columns, several crosses.',!1)
B.CC=new A.bd("Work the lower blocks. The blocks pairing categories against each other are not decoration \u2014 they are where most of the puzzle gets solved. If a clue tells you about an item and a place without naming a person, that is where it goes.",!1)
B.C0=new A.bd("Follow a mark through. If Ivy Marsh was at the millpond, and the millpond goes with the seed tin, then Ivy Marsh had the seed tin. Every confirmation is worth chasing across the grid before you read on.",!1)
B.C6=new A.bd("A row with every cell crossed is a mistake, not a discovery. Every row and column ends with exactly one confirmation. If one has none left, something earlier was wrong \u2014 undo back rather than pressing on.",!1)
B.Cd=new A.bd("When you are stuck, re-read the clue you understood least. It is almost always the one carrying the step you have not taken.",!1)
B.EI=s([B.Ct,B.CC,B.C0,B.C6,B.Cd],t.T9)
B.BT=new A.iG("Tips and techniques",B.EI)
B.Ca=new A.bd("Three things are true of every case in this app, and they are checked by machine before the case is ever shipped.",!1)
B.Cx=new A.bd("Exactly one solution",!0)
B.BY=new A.bd('Not "we believe" \u2014 counted. The generator draws an answer first, writes only clues that are true of it, then counts solutions until exactly one remains.',!1)
B.Cg=new A.bd("Not one clue you do not need",!0)
B.Cr=new A.bd("Every clue is tested for removal. If the case survives without it, it is cut.",!1)
B.C2=new A.bd("You never have to guess",!0)
B.C7=new A.bd('This one is worth explaining, because it is not the same as the first. A puzzle can have exactly one answer and still be unreachable \u2014 you cross off everything the clues allow and stop, with no forced next mark and no way on except "suppose it was her\u2026 no\u2026 then it wasn\'t". That is guessing with extra steps.',!1)
B.BZ=new A.bd("So a second solver checks every case, restricted on purpose to what a person does with a pencil: crossing off, one mark per row and column, and following a mark through. It never assumes anything. If it stalls, the case is not shipped.",!1)
B.Fk=s([B.Ca,B.Cx,B.BY,B.Cg,B.Cr,B.C2,B.C7,B.BZ],t.T9)
B.BS=new A.iG("About these puzzles",B.Fk)
B.CD=new A.bd("Do I need an internet connection?",!0)
B.Cn=new A.bd("No. Every case is inside the app. Nothing is fetched, nothing is uploaded, nothing is measured about you.",!1)
B.C3=new A.bd("Are there ads?",!0)
B.Cq=new A.bd("No, and there will not be.",!1)
B.CA=new A.bd("Will I be asked to pay?",!0)
B.C1=new A.bd("No. Every case in the app is free. If you want more of them, they exist as paperbacks.",!1)
B.Cc=new A.bd("Does my progress save?",!0)
B.Ch=new A.bd("Yes, and mid-case. Leave a case half-marked, close the app, come back to it.",!1)
B.Cv=new A.bd("Can I replay a solved case?",!0)
B.Cp=new A.bd("Yes. Open it and clear the grid.",!1)
B.CB=new A.bd("Can two cases be the same?",!0)
B.Cm=new A.bd("No. Every case has its own clues and its own answer.",!1)
B.Cj=new A.bd("I think a case is wrong.",!0)
B.Ci=new A.bd("Then we want to know, and it would be the first. Tell us and we will check it against the generator.",!1)
B.Fj=s([B.CD,B.Cn,B.C3,B.Cq,B.CA,B.C1,B.Cc,B.Ch,B.Cv,B.Cp,B.CB,B.Cm,B.Cj,B.Ci],t.T9)
B.BW=new A.iG("Questions",B.Fj)
B.C5=new A.bd("The village of Thistledown has more cases than fit in a phone app, and they are made for paper: large print, big grids, no battery, no subscription.",!1)
B.Cl=new A.bd("Grids the size of the ones on paper simply do not fit on a phone comfortably. That is what the books are for.",!1)
B.Eq=s([B.C5,B.Cl],t.T9)
B.BU=new A.iG("The books",B.Eq)
B.EP=s([B.BV,B.BX,B.BT,B.BS,B.BW,B.BU],A.ai("B<iG>"))
